## 3. Architecture & Data Flow

```
[ Client Browser ]
        │
        │ 1. POST /api/submissions (Code, ProblemId, Lang)
        ▼
[ Express API Server ]  (Fast I/O Bound)
        │
        ├─► 2. Save Submission in PostgreSQL (status = 'QUEUED')
        ├─► 3. Enqueue Job into Redis Queue (BullMQ Producer)
        │
        ▼ 4. Immediate HTTP 201 Created { id, status: 'QUEUED' } (10-15 ms)
[ Client Browser ]  (Starts polling GET /api/submissions/:id)
        │
        │
================= ASYNCHRONOUS BOUNDARY (REDIS) =================
        │
        ▼ 5. Worker dequeues job via blocking Redis connection (BLMOVE)
[ Worker Process ] (src/worker.ts - CPU/Compute Bound)
        │
        ├─► 6. Update status = 'RUNNING' in PostgreSQL
        ├─► 7. Launch Docker Sandbox (`--cpus=1.0`, `--memory=256m`, `--network=none`)
        ├─► 8. Compile (if C++/Java), feed test cases via stdin, evaluate stdout
        ├─► 9. Update status = 'ACCEPTED'/'WRONG_ANSWER'/etc. in PostgreSQL
        │
        ▼ 10. Mark job COMPLETED in Redis
```

